<figure id="A5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08338v1/Fig06.svg" id="A5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:438/276;" width="438" height="276"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6. </span>Comparison of real and synthetic surveys based on Gem-2f with <math id="A5.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{LLM}}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>LLM</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{LLM}}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A5.F6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A)</span> Mean purchase intent comparison for <span id="A5.F6.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A.i)</span> Direct likert ratings (DLRs), <span id="A5.F6.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A.ii)</span> textual elicitation with follow-up Likert ratings (FLRs) and <span id="A5.F6.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(A.iii)</span> semantic similarity ratings (SSRs). <span id="A5.F6.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(B)</span> Eight example survey response distributions for real surveys and the corresponding synthetic surveys based on DLR, FLR, and SSR, respectively.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.08338v1/Fig07.svg" id="A5.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:191/191;" width="191" height="191"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7. </span>Comparison of purchase intent distribution similarity between real and synthetic surveys based on Gem-2f with <math id="A5.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\mathrm{LLM}}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>LLM</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\mathrm{LLM}}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> for direct Likert ratings (DLRs), textual elicitation with follow-up Likert ratings (FLRs), semantic similarity ratings (SSRs), and best-set SSRs for an experiment where synthetic consumers where prompted without demographic markers.</figcaption>
</figure>
